config HCP_BENCH
	bool "Bench / HIL firmware: bring-up aids on, verbose logging"
	default n
	help
	  A build meant to be run on the test bench rather than shipped: the periodic
	  Modbus poll is compiled in, the raw UART loopback self-test can be turned on
	  beside it, and device-domain logging is debug so the boot is readable
	  without a serial session. hcp::provision, MQTT, SSDP and OTA stay in, so a
	  bench device is reachable and upgradeable over the network - which is the
	  point: after the first flash it should never need the USB port again.

	  ./build.sh <board> --bench

	  The LED colour cycle needs the strip to itself, so it only compiles when
	  hcp::provision is off (a status light and a demo cannot share one pin). For a
	  BLE-and-LED-only image, add -DCONFIG_HCP_PROVISION=n.

	  The raw UART loopback self-test is NOT part of the bench default: it talks on
	  the same uart1 the Modbus poll uses, so the two would fight for the port.
	  Enable it on its own (-DCONFIG_HCP_SERIAL_LOOPBACK_TEST=y) when checking
	  wiring, with the poll off.

	  The product build compiles none of this in, and the boot banner says which
	  image is running.

config APP_VERSION
	string "firmware version (dotted numeric: major.minor.patch)"
	default "0.1.0"
	help
	  The one version knob of a build. Reported on the <sn>/online topic and used
	  by hcp::ota as "what am I running", so an update is only taken when the
	  server offers something above it. MCUboot compares the version in the image
	  header (CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMGTOOL_SIGN_VERSION), not this string, so the two
	  have to move together: ./build.sh <board> --version <x.y.z> sets both.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
